    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. There's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`); the other two files are the abstract base and the capture helper.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**New file** \u2014 `rest/OwnerAuditLogger.java`: a small `@Component` with a single responsibility, owning the audit-logging concern. It logs to the dedicated `AUDIT` logger (via SLF4J) an owner-created line carrying the owner **id**, **customerCode**, and **registrationDate**.\n\n**Wired into** `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`: injected `OwnerAuditLogger` via the constructor and call `ownerAuditLogger.ownerCreated(owner)` immediately after `saveOwner(...)` succeeds \u2014 so the id, generated customer code, and business-day-resolved registration date are all populated when logged.\n\nI kept the audit logic out of the controller rather than inlining a logger there, so the controller stays focused on request handling and the audit behavior lives in its own reusable unit.\n\nResult: `AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-16`, and `BUILD SUCCESS` with all tests passing.",
